   $q$The narrator says the crack "was a sentence she had written herself, weeks ago, in a language she was only beginning to read." What does this metaphor suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The crack records her own technique, which she is learning to interpret.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Priya had secretly carved words into the clay as she shaped it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Priya struggles with her English class as well as with pottery.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"The crack was caused by the kiln, which Priya could not control.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The crack records her own technique, which she is learning to interpret.$q$, $q$The crack traces back to the thin wall left when "her trimming tool had slipped," so it is a record of her own work, and the "language" is the skill of reading what clay shows. The narrator explicitly says the crack "was not a curse from the kiln."$q$, 'draft', '26d626ff-d221-5dbe-8f99-4fd15162e07d')
