  ('722427a6-9acb-51fa-b684-fdbe93a4feff', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The passage ends: "He had spent a month trying to carry the boat, and the boat had only wanted him to let it carry him." What is the effect of reversing "carry" in this sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It hints that Tomas will quit the team because rowing felt too easy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows his shift from forcing results alone to trusting the shared rhythm.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It explains that the boat is light enough for one rower to lift and carry.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It suggests Tomas was too tired to row, so the crew had to row for him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows his shift from forcing results alone to trusting the shared rhythm.$q$, $q$The reversal mirrors his realization: straining to power the boat alone failed, while syncing with the crew let the boat "run" and his legs "burned less." He was not exhausted or carried by others; he rowed in rhythm with them.$q$, 'draft', '82ef284f-3030-5958-9564-1bbb52a0a775')
