   $q$Station clocks hung side by side, "each one insisting on a different hour." What does "insisting" suggest about the clocks?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The clocks were broken and kept stopping at random times.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"All the clocks agreed and showed the same exact hour.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Each clock firmly showed its own time, creating a clash.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Station workers argued loudly about which clock was right.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Each clock firmly showed its own time, creating a clash.$q$, $q$Giving the clocks a stubborn human quality stresses that each displayed a different time with equal authority, which confused travelers. The passage says the hours were "different," so the clocks did not agree.$q$, 'draft', '5b4a954b-e234-57ca-8bbc-c282b017bb02')
