values
  ('15feb412-7553-5205-8a8f-34bde9c12878', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-figurative-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Over-compressed images show "blocky squares" that "bloom across the sky." What does "bloom" suggest about these flaws?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They make the photo look brighter and more colorful.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-connotation"},{"text":"They spread and appear across the image as it degrades.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They disappear slowly the more times a file is saved.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They appear only in photos of gardens and flowers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They spread and appear across the image as it degrades.$q$, $q$Like flowers opening, the squares emerge and spread when an image is squeezed "too hard" or saved "again and again." The passage says repeated saving causes the flaws, so they do not fade with saving.$q$, 'draft', '823c1dda-3228-5a71-bc05-911744b562c3')
