   $q$The software "keeps the details our eyes guard most closely." What does "guard most closely" mean in this context?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Details that are protected by passwords on the phone","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Details that the camera sensor fails to capture at all","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Details that human vision is most sensitive to noticing","is_correct":true},{"text":"Details that people try to hide from others in their photos","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning-in-context"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Details that human vision is most sensitive to noticing$q$, $q$The paragraph explains that we notice brightness changes and "sharp edges more readily," so the details our eyes "guard" are the ones we would notice if they changed. The phrase is about perception, not privacy.$q$, 'draft', '823c1dda-3228-5a71-bc05-911744b562c3')
