  ('8fa65822-fff3-5fac-930e-8d49be01896f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Kwame calls the night "a total, complete, absolute waste," and Ms. Delacroix notes he has "used three words that mean the same thing." What is the effect of this stacked hyperbole?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Ms. Delacroix agrees the trip was a failure.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It shows Kwame is trying to teach the club new vocabulary.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It proves the night truly was wasted from start to finish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows his overreaction, which she gently points out is premature.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows his overreaction, which she gently points out is premature.$q$, $q$Piling up three synonyms exaggerates his disappointment, and her reply that "none of them are true yet" signals the night is not over. The meteors and laughter that follow prove the night was not wasted.$q$, 'draft', '644ac0f9-9f8b-5995-bbe1-d02e8ddd4f9b')
