   $q$Years of light can "turn white paper the color of weak tea." What does this simile describe?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The paper turns bright white after years on display.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The paper becomes soft and wet as it absorbs light.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Museums stain old paper with tea to make it look antique.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The paper fades to a pale yellowish brown over time.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The paper fades to a pale yellowish brown over time.$q$, $q$Weak tea is a pale brownish color, so the simile shows how light discolors once white paper. The passage describes light damage, not anyone deliberately staining paper.$q$, 'draft', 'c0a43c5b-a0c3-5bed-9f55-c4629ce0a585')
