   $q$The author asks readers to "consider the dim lighting a kind of courtesy." What does "courtesy" suggest about the lighting?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is a rule that visitors must follow to avoid being fined.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It is a way for museums to save money on their electric bills.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"It is an unfortunate accident that museums have not yet fixed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It is a considerate choice made with others' interests in mind.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is a considerate choice made with others' interests in mind.$q$, $q$A courtesy is a polite, thoughtful act, and the next sentences show the dimness protects works for "visitors who have not been born yet." The passage presents low light as deliberate, so it is not an accident.$q$, 'draft', 'c0a43c5b-a0c3-5bed-9f55-c4629ce0a585')
